# GISclaw — optional environment configuration.
#
# You do NOT need this file: API keys can be pasted in the app under
# Settings → API keys…, where they are stored server-side under
# <your data folder>/.gisclaw/settings.json (mode 600) and survive rebuilds.
#
# Use this file instead if you prefer keys to come from the environment
# (CI, shared hosts, secret managers). Values here act as the fallback.


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where your work is kept. Worth setting on day one.
#
# Everything you produce — projects, data, outputs, run history, and the keys
# entered in the interface — lives in this folder on your own disk.
#
# Left unset it is ./projects, inside this source folder. That works, but the
# source folder is the thing you replace when a new version comes out, and
# deleting it would take your work with it. Point this somewhere separate and
# the source folder becomes disposable:
#
#     GISCLAW_DATA=/home/you/GISclaw-data       (Linux / macOS)
#     GISCLAW_DATA=C:\Users\you\GISclaw-data    (Windows)
#
# Move any existing ./projects there first, then `docker compose up -d`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GISCLAW_DATA=

# OpenAI                      https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Anthropic (Claude)          https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
CLAUDE_API_KEY=

# DeepSeek — cheapest, good for trying things out
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=

# Google Gemini               https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Optional: an extra local skills directory to load bundles from.
# Never point this at someone else's skill collection in a published image.
# GISCLAW_EXTRA_SKILLS=/path/to/skills

# Optional: workspace root inside the container (default /workspace).
# GISCLAW_WORKSPACE=/workspace
